    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0551" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg379"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 832.30/22</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-03T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 3, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your December 1, 12 noon, and December 2, 12 noon.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d556-f1"
                    /> Navy Department ready to comply with request of Brazilian Government us to
                    five naval officers; names will be cabled as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to present cordial invitation to Brazilian Government to send
                    squadron of destroyers to join American naval forces now operating against the
                    enemy. Navy Department has communicated with Admiral Sims in London in regard to
                    disposal <pb facs="0552" n="380" xml:id="pg380"/> of Brazilian squadron, if
                    invitation is accepted. You will be informed immediately upon receipt of his
                    reply. Probable disposition southern waters.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
